course: dictionary
lesson: 14114
title: Meteorology: the science of weather
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meteorology is the science of the weather and the atmosphere. The atmosphere is the layer of air around the Earth. A scientist who studies it is called a meteorologist.
explain: Meteorologists study air, temperature, wind, clouds and rain. They use what they learn to understand the weather and predict what it will do next. «Ella wants to study meteorology when she grows up.» Ella wants to learn the science behind the weather, not just read a forecast.
explain: Look at the clues in a sentence. «The meteorologist said rain would arrive by noon.» Meteorologist is a person, and the sentence is about rain and forecasts, so meteorology must be the science that studies weather.
fact: Meteorology means the science of the weather.
fact: A meteorologist is a scientist who studies meteorology.
fact: Meteorologists use thermometers, rain gauges, barometers, weather balloons, satellites and computer models.
fact: National weather services such as the Met Office (UK) and the Bureau of Meteorology (Australia) use meteorology to make forecasts.
fact: Phrase: «study meteorology» means to learn about the science of weather.
exercise: «Ella wants to study meteorology.» What does meteorology mean? | The study of animals and plants | The study of rocks deep under the ground | The study of old castles and buildings | *The science of the weather and the atmosphere
exercise: A meteorologist uses a rain gauge. What does a rain gauge measure? | How fast a car moves | How old a tree is | *How much rain falls
exercise: «The Bureau of Meteorology issued a storm warning.» Which country does the Bureau of Meteorology belong to? | Egypt | *Australia | France | Japan
test: «The meteorologist said rain would arrive by noon.» Who is a meteorologist? | *A scientist who studies the weather | A doctor who checks the rain | A person who sells umbrellas
test: Which tool do meteorologists use to measure air pressure? | A thermometer | A rain gauge | A microscope | *A barometer
exam: Which of these is NOT a tool used in meteorology? | A weather balloon | A satellite | *A microscope | A thermometer
